I'm just noting this down by ear from the TV show aired, the song hasn't been put onto YouTube or
anywhere yet so I don't know about the bridge or other verses. I'm not sure about the lyric on
the line:
"I been a slow and silent dancer to a rhythm that's impure" so forgive me if it's incorrect but
everything else should be ok. If the Am sounds off then just sub in Em for them.
I tried this on piano and the Am with inversion (E A C) worked well so I put it in.
This is played in standard tuning (i.e. no capo) but obviously put one on if you want to sing it
higher
